<title>USA: Dow, Nasdaq firm at open after U.S. jobs data.</title>
<headline>Dow, Nasdaq firm at open after U.S. jobs data.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dow industrials nudged higher and the Nasdaq composite also rose at Friday's open, following release of data which showed the U.S. unemployment rate fell to 4.8 percent in May, with 138,000 new jobs added.</p>
<p>The Dow Industrials was up 15.45 at 7320.74. The 30-year long bond off 8/32 to yield 6.90 percent.</p>
</text>
